content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line (sodium hypochlorite dosed)",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration at the drive-end bearing housing is 7.6 mm/s. The applicable limit is HF-300 Figure 3: Zone D starts at 7.1 mm/s RMS and is marked 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. The reading is 0.5 mm/s into Zone D. Per section 3, the highest bearing-housing reading sets the action, so the pump must be stopped.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 84 C. The applicable limits are in the HF-300 specification table: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C. The reading is 4 C above alarm and 6 C below trip. It is measured on the housing surface, as the manual specifies.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Water is leaking from the shaft area at about 1 drop per second. The manual gives no numeric leakage limit. The troubleshooting table lists shaft-seal leakage as a symptom that calls for mechanical seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The pump ran dry for about 10 minutes last week. This breaches the manual requirement that the Plan 11 seal flush comes from pump discharge and the pump is never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal faces damaged by the roughly 10-minute dry run. 'Seal run dry' is a listed cause of shaft-seal leakage, and the fitted seal relies on a Plan 11 flush that is lost when the pump runs dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Early failure of the original component seal HF3-450. Field returns show early failures on serials HF3-22000 and above because of a revised sleeve tolerance, and this pump (HF3-22871) is in that range.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear, possibly made worse by the dry-run event. Bearing wear is a listed cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is the only listed cause common to all three symptoms: seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Other possible contributors: over-greasing (high bearing temperature), and impeller imbalance or damage or cavitation (high vibration).",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop pump P-104 immediately, because vibration is in Zone D. Do not restart until repairs are complete.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. The line is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite, so treat the drained water and wetted parts as chemically contaminated.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly using lifting equipment, because it weighs 68 kg. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller. Inspect the impeller for damage or imbalance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the old seal and shaft sleeve. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3). This is required because drive-end temperature is above alarm and vibration indicates possible wear. Check grease quantity to rule out over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B (do NOT fit HF3-450). HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve setting measurement is needed. Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten fasteners on lightly oiled threads to: casing bolts M16 210 Nm; impeller nut M24 160 Nm; bearing housing bolts M12 85 Nm; seal gland nuts M10 30 Nm (per SB-2026-014, not the 25 Nm in Table 5).",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the shaft, because the bearing housing has been disturbed. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, fill and vent the casing so the pump is never run dry, and confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from discharge is working. Check NPSH and suction conditions to rule out cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading against Figure 3. Target Zone A/B (at or below 4.5 mm/s RMS). Confirm bearing housing temperature returns to the normal range of 70 C or below.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replaced as a pair with DE)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, CONDITIONAL: fit only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth; have one on hand",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump now. A Zone D reading means 'Damage likely - stop the pump'.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before starting work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The filtered-water line is dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Treat the drained fluid and wetted parts as chemical hazards.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Prime it and confirm the Plan 11 seal flush before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Standard times total 11.5 h if done sequentially, using 2 technicians for seal and bearing work and 1 for alignment. Overlap savings are not documented.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number: the manual parts list (Rev D) specifies component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes it with cartridge seal HF3-450B for serial HF3-22000 and above. P-104 is serial HF3-22871, which is in that range, so HF3-450B applies and HF3-450 must not be fitted.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. The bulletin covers this serial and states that only pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use Table 5 for the seal, so 30 Nm applies. All other Table 5 torques remain valid.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve check: manual 5.2 calls for sleeve inspection as part of the seal fit, while the bulletin says no sleeve measurement is needed because HF3-450B is pre-set. Scoring must still be checked, and the sleeve replaced if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. The bulletin applies to this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the 7.6 mm/s reading RMS velocity, as Figure 3 assumes? What is the non-drive-end bearing housing reading?",
    "What are the site PPE, decontamination and drain-disposal requirements for sodium hypochlorite? SSP-07 only states that the line is dosed.",
    "What grease type and quantity apply to the bearings? Not covered in the evidence.",
    "Lockout/isolation procedure details and permit requirements for P-104 are not provided.",
    "No numeric acceptable seal leakage rate is documented.",
    "Should the impeller be replaced, and do wear rings need checking after the dry run? Criteria are not specified.",
    "Is there a site- or OEM-specific requirement to inspect for other dry-run damage beyond the seal? Not covered.",
    "Total crew time when tasks overlap is not documented.",
    "Are spare HF3-450B, the bearings and HF3-455 available in stores? Not covered."
  ]
}
